[2] SUPPORT FLOOR consequence (z=0, full-support relations in Z^k):
    A relation with ALL k coords nonzero contributes iff its offsets' Fourier
    assignment can hit all 6 sectors. For k>=6 this is possible; for the lattice
    Lambda^o(E) the SHORT vectors are typically support 2-3 (e_a*p = e_b*q etc.),
    which by the collapse have z=k-supp large => need image >= 6-z, easy, BUT the
    short vectors with support 2 ALWAYS give image<=2 <= 6-z requires z<=4 i.e. k<=6.
      k=7: support-2 vector has z=5; needs sector-image >= 1. image of 2 coords <= 2, so contributes only if 1<=2 i.e. k>=6=6. => support-2 CAN contribute at k=7.
      k=8: support-2 vector has z=6; needs sector-image >= 0. image of 2 coords <= 2, so contributes only if 0<=2 i.e. k>=6=6. => support-2 CAN contribute at k=8.
      k=9: support-2 vector has z=7; needs sector-image >= -1. image of 2 coords <= 2, so contributes only if -1<=2 i.e. k>=6=6. => support-2 CAN contribute at k=9.
    (Matches angleF: support-2 had nonzero SIGNED partials at k=8 because z=6,
     need=image>=0, i.e. ALL assignments survive when there are >=6 zero-coords.)

