[4] COVERING-SIEVE identity for FULL-SUPPORT relations (z=0):
    K(n) = (-1)^k sum_{R subset {1..6}} (-1)^{6-|R|} prod_j (sum_{s in R} shat(n_j,s))
    = the inclusion-exclusion sieve for COVERING all 6 inner sectors -- the SAME
    sieve as meas(S7) (cover all 7 sectors), one dimension down (7-vanishing kills
    sector 0). The kernel is RECURSIVELY a covering problem.
    full-support covering-sieve identity VERIFIED, max err = 0.00e+00

[5] THE supp=2 DEFICIT (the one stratum consec does NOT maximize):
    supp-2 relations = pairwise commensurabilities e_i/e_j = -b/a (the lambda_1
    short vectors). Deep truncation (N0=40) confirms perf8 > consec here:
      consec8: supp-2 signed contribution (N0=40) = +0.02506
      perf8: supp-2 signed contribution (N0=40) = +0.02791
    => This is exactly the WALL-ALIGNMENT stratum (Route A): the supp-2 commensur-
    abilities are the scale-1/7-grid resonances that T(x) is blind to. consec is NOT
    supp-2-maximal, so Route G does NOT close per-stratum. consec WINS on supp 3..7
    (proved-dominant in [3]) and the supp-2 deficit must be repaid by the higher
    strata -- a genuinely JOINT cancellation (matches HYP-2607 non-separability).

