READOUT
======================================================================================
PROVED (exact): the kernel COLLAPSES. K(n)=sum over sector-assignments of the
nonzero coords, weighted by c(z,|image|), with the HARD floor c(z,s)=0 for s<6-z.
The sign (-1)^|T| is fully integrated out; the 7-vanishing becomes a support floor
(#zeros)+(min image)=6. This is a real structural simplification of Route G's object.
COVERING-SIEVE (proved [4]): full-support K(n) = (-1)^k * [signed sieve covering all
6 inner sectors] -- the meas(S7) cover-7 sieve, recursively, one dim down (7-vanishing).
PARTIAL Route-G reduction (proved [3],[5], EXACT/numeric to truncation): consec
DOMINATES the signed kernel stratum at support 3,4,5,6,7; it loses ONLY at support 2
(the wall-alignment commensurability stratum). So consec-extremality of the signed
correction is NOT per-stratum -- the supp-2 deficit must be repaid by consec's higher-
support surplus (JOINT cancellation, HYP-2607). The open piece is exactly this one
low-stratum repayment, now ISOLATED to the lambda_1 (shortest commensurability) shell.
DONE.
